{"seq":20,"trial_id":"anatomy-instruction-route-2026-11/hermes-haiku-gbrain-route-startup-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T18:37:30.031Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"a85a98296a1ba7024be07d5be7303b8d4668254e2c727c3e9c2a7512e68a6b31","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DANATOM0001","text":"Hi Dana, here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. #PD-4492: Pemberline Dock gatehouse kiosk alerts at the Eau Claire yard (drivers for the 04:00 shift at Doors 14-18 not getting SMS bay assignments). Thea Ramaswell submitted it 4 Oct 2025. Source: teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md (\"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\"), What Changed section. That digest says Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct 2025.\n\n2. #4419: gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. Source: teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md (\"Moss: North cheat sheet\", undated), Account & Operational Notes. Its What Changed section says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nNotes:\n- Marcus Lindqvist's note (members/marcus-lindqvist/notes/2025-07-14-marcus-q2-expansion-wrap.md) also cites #4419, but for a different issue (Gate 3 printer lag). It isn't one of Moss's notes, so I left it out of the list, but the two descriptions don't match, so it's worth checking which is right.\n- #4409 and #4412 are in Moss's Central handoffs digest, but they belong to Pree's dealer account, not Quarrendon, so I left them out.\n\nI can't edit the weekly notes file myself. I can post this in #north-team or draft it to Ruth if you want that."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DANATOM0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
